{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image","id":666436,"title":"Just one Changeling wish: Fix the Unseelie Image!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-15T21:19:00-07:00","id":666436,"title":"Just one Changeling wish: Fix the Unseelie Image!","content":"We all here about how Unseelie does not necessarily mean evil, but we all know in the game, they are always the bad guys along with a few hyper traditionalist Seelie tyrants. I want some actual Unseelie motlys where the Unseelie are the good guys. Ones who care about others, who aren't running around stalking children like a pedo as they wait for a chance to ravage them along with other innocents, who are genuinely working towards a positive goal. Perhaps they are ravaging corporate lobbyists and human traffickers for glamour. Perhaps they are reeking havoc in institutions that deserve to burn. Perhaps there style is constructive destruction and are being nightmares to people who genuinely deserve to have them. Instead all we get are story examples about your characters having to protect hapless dreamers from the shortsighted Unseelie for the greater good of the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T23:28:37-07:00","id":666519,"title":"","content":"I'd take it even farther myself:<br /> <br /> Get rid of the idea that most changelings are either Seelie or Unseelie. Have the default assumption be that most changelings will flip fairly regularly. This, generally speaking, helps fix the Unseelie image because it's pretty hard to paint all of them as evil if most changelings spend a good portion of their lives in that state. You shift the negative perceptions to changelings that completely eschew one side of their nature. Always being on one side or the other being what the majority of fae society distrusts lets you keep the baby-eating super nasty Unseelie and the hyper-traditionalist tyrannical Seelie examples as exactly why such individuals aren't trusted.<br /> <br /> If C20 is written in the mindset that PC changelings will be changing regularly enough, it helps make sure the Unseelie aren't too heavily slammed in their presentation because they need to present things players are going to want to do who aren't already into playing a nightmarish goblin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T03:09:13-07:00","id":666664,"title":"","content":"It could be interesting to have a mechanic for flipping between legacies. If a character is too heroic, he might flip to Seelie. A character who witnesses atrocities and is marked by them might flip to Unseelie. It needn't be much more than an optional rule in a sidebar, but it might add an interesting dimension to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T05:16:40-07:00","id":666772,"title":"","content":"All good ideas. Frankly, the Unseelie were so badly handled, I would just settle for a Krampus at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:03:36-07:00","id":667078,"title":"","content":"The problem is the Seelie Code either can be interpretted as very White or very Orange in a moral context. Lets look at the code.<br /> <br /> Death Before Dishonor-This lets you play up chivalry or the twisted nature of Fae who cannot let go of something no matter what.<br /> Love Conquers all-It sounds nice and romantic but it is also the call of the crazy monster stalker<br /> beauty is life-This one sounds good but the more you think about it the more ambiguous it can be taken.<br /> Never Forget a Debt-Once more Chivalric knight or twisted fae unable to let things go.<br /> <br /> The Seelie code is well rounded letting you play super nice characters and monsters with equal aplomb and neither is &quot;doing it wrong&quot;. More to the point while Musing is the official position of the Seelie as a political statement nothing in the code keeps you from being the Ravager who feeds on humans who oath breakers, taking what it owed to you!<br /> <br /> Now lets look at the Unseelie code which varies from tennents that are morally ambiguous to objectively wrong in a setting sense to actively coming off as evil.<br /> <br /> Change is good-This is ambiguous there are times people can see change as necissary but for the most part people are abhorrent to change. Still its the world of Darkness this can a bright spot as someone who wants to rewrite all the the rules.<br /> <br /> Glamour is Free-Full stop this is bullshit. Its fundimentally runs up against the setting conceit of Glamour being rare and dying. This makes every Unseelie member at best wasteful in a dying world and this is before we point to Ravaging and Rapturing for litterally killing the Golden Goose.<br /> <br /> Honor is a lie-House Ailil does a wonderful job ruleslawyering the shit out of why this isn't as horrible as it sounds. But its House Ailil. It takes a lot to move this out of the dark grey to black category.<br /> <br /> Passion before duty-this one definately comes off as sinister but can be interpretted as benign, however much like Honor is a lie and Glamour is free it seems to fly in the face of setting rules.<br /> <br /> To make the Unseelie valid afew things have to change either the code in general or a couple things to make the code abit less screwed. My first thought is make Ravaging more morally ambiguous, right now gaining Glamour from it is the equivalent of if Vampire had two options of gaining blood, one which ruined peoples lives and made them never able to bleed again and the other which had blood just magically appear from heaven by divine fiat.<br /> <br /> So make Glamour harvesting from humans less objectively killing the Dreaming would go a long way towards making Glamour is free a more valid statement.<br /> <br /> Next we have Oaths. Oaths are so important the Dreaming backs them yet &quot;Honor is a lie&quot; and &quot;passion before duty&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally we have objectively evil mirrors of kiths that are pure unseelie. <br /> <br /> <br /> So how would I fix this? I'd rewrite the last 3 tenents of the code to be more a moral statement and less a &quot;Do whatever the fuck you want, no consequences&quot;. I'd make Glamour harvests from humans more of the norm and less obviously killing the dreaming and drop the Thalain unless we're going to see some super evil Seelie only variants as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:14:51-07:00","id":667099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=667078#post667078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of good things. However, the one thing i do want to correct you on is honor is a lie being evil. After all societies with honor often have things like: Honor Killings, Blood fueds, Honor sucides, Duels, among other things.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I am not really familar with changeling, but hopefully c20 will help with me better understanding this game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:41:09-07:00","id":667602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=667099#post667099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of good things. However, the one thing i do want to correct you on is honor is a lie being evil. After all societies with honor often have things like: Honor Killings, Blood fueds, Honor sucides, Duels, among other things.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I am not really familar with changeling, but hopefully c20 will help with me better understanding this game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My issue is two fold, first it not really a prescriptive point. It just kind of causes Unseelie to be jerks ESPECIALLY to whole kiths who are built around Honor.<br /> <br /> Plus like Glamour is free this is treated in setting as objectively wrong. Honor is a real metaphysical law in the dreaming it would be abit like if the Camarilla had a Tradition that said &quot;Thermodynamics is a lie&quot;<br /> <br /> I might combine Passion before duty and Honor is a lie into something more like &quot;Honor is Personal&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T19:21:17-07:00","id":667724,"title":"","content":"*Wild Applause* Well done, Lian! This sums up perfectly what is wrong with the Unseelie. Especially the &quot;Glamour is Free&quot; part. It's like having &quot;Climate Change is a Hoax&quot; as part of their code. It's telling a race of beings who who live off of a special environment, like fish and water, to actively disregard any and all damage they actively do to that environment. Maybe the guy who wrote the Unseelie Code was the Dick Cheney of the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T22:22:50-07:00","id":667828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=667724#post667724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Wild Applause* Well done, Lian! This sums up perfectly what is wrong with the Unseelie. Especially the &quot;Glamour is Free&quot; part. It's like having &quot;Climate Change is a Hoax&quot; as part of their code. It's telling a race of beings who who live off of a special environment, like fish and water, to actively disregard any and all damage they actively do to that environment. Maybe the guy who wrote the Unseelie Code was the Dick Cheney of the Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its not just they are the crazy climate change faction but they are the crazy climate change faction in a game where you signed up to play about Climate change and resource management in the face of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Really the Unseelie need to be more than just &quot;that reasonable part you repress because monster&quot; playing up the Values of Freedom, the glamour of nightmares, that things of horror, things of rage are as much of the Dreaming and shattering someone's bland comfortable banality as things of beauty. At its best when people look at the Unseelie they should see activists who want to change the world, at its worst they are just terrorists who want to see things burn.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T23:31:07-07:00","id":667865,"title":"","content":".Of note is that for pretty much every type of fae outside the Kithain and Thallain, they dropped the idea of Codes. The other fae have a division in their natures (in the adhene's case, a three-way division), but they don't have Codes that each side of the division is expected to uphold.<br /> <br /> Also, reading through the Nunnehi writeup in the Players Guide, switching between Summer and Winter Camps is a recognised and accepted thing when it comes necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T00:07:27-07:00","id":667938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=667865#post667865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.Of note is that for pretty much every type of fae outside the Kithain and Thallain, they dropped the idea of Codes. The other fae have a division in their natures (in the adhene's case, a three-way division), but they don't have Codes that each side of the division is expected to uphold.<br /> <br /> Also, reading through the Nunnehi writeup in the Players Guide, switching between Summer and Winter Camps is a recognised and accepted thing when it comes necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there's greater value to having an alien moral and political setup for it rather than &quot;sometimes you become an asshole&quot; which is really what the random swapping stuff ends up saying. It doesn't make the other side seem as important to the Dreaming its really just asshole Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T05:09:32-07:00","id":668087,"title":"","content":"I read all of the Unseelie code very differently, I guess. It strikes me more as an individualistic, non-hierarchical code.<br /> <br /> 'Glamour is free' means, to me, that Glamour should belong to everyone. Glamour shouldn't be rationed and hoarded. It should be shared and spent and used. However, I agree that Ravaging needs to be less objectively evil in the setting. It should be possible to Ravage someone but for them to recover and dream again. I'd perhaps make it more like Changeling: The Lost, where you can inspire an emotion in someone and feed off that, as a baser form of Glamour reaping. It's how wraiths feed (sort of), so it wouldn't be completely out of place in the setting. The side-effects for the victim could range from temporary madness to inertia to a deep, nightmarish sleep, so that there were still consequences, but ones which don't kill the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> 'Honour is a lie' - well, it's kind of true, isn't it? Yes, oaths have an objective existence as magical ties to the Dreaming, but they're also a kind of voluntary servitude or even enslavement. Following an oath becomes less about honour, for me, and more about lack of freedom. You're coerced into following oaths, because there are serious metaphysical penalties for not doing so. True honour would be following a vow to someone or following a cause without supernatural forces pushing you to do so. I'd propose, instead, a system of vows to mirror the system of oaths. These would be agreements freely entered into, but which have no mechanical or metaphysical component. They're things the Unseelie want to do, rather than things they have to do. I'd have them be roleplaying concepts only (like Nature and Demeanour), but you could always allow them to provide social bonuses - especially if you port in the Social Combat rules from Dead Man's Party.<br /> <br /> 'Passion before duty' is also a pretty Romantic, anti-authoritarian and highly individualistic concept. It reminds me of Crowley's tenet 'Do as thou wilt shall be the whole of the law'. In other words, do a thing because you feel passionately about it, and because you want to do it, not because of guilt, shame or moral obligation. That might seem selfish, and it probably is by most counts, but it's also being truer to yourself. There's a different kind of honour, subjectively, in being true to yourself and your own ideals, rather than to the status quo. For that reason, I'd recommend that Unseelie characters note down passions that they have. When following these passions, I'd give them the opportunity to regain Glamour or Willpower (to balance it out, I'd also reward the following of oaths with the same for Seelie characters). You could port in the Passions system from Wraith if you really wanted to get crunchy, otherwise you can just list three core passions and issue Glamour or Willpower as feels appropriate. (Another option might instead be to allow a reroll on any action that directly feeds or follows a passion.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 09-17-2015, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T05:10:08-07:00","id":668088,"title":"","content":"In fact, I may submit these suggestions to Onyx Path directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T06:43:50-07:00","id":668173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=668088#post668088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I may submit these suggestions to Onyx Path directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do, I recommend sending it as a writing sample instead of as a suggestion for C20. The game's been sitting in the first draft stage in the Monday Meeting notes for awhile now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Edit to add:</b> As for ravaging, I like it being an easy way to get glamour that might damage the dreamer and is a little risky for the changeling. There's nothing saying an unseelie can't use horror or anger to actually muse someone. Glamour is passion, and there's just as much passion in negative emotions as positive ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 09-17-2015, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:36:14-07:00","id":668236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=667938#post667938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's greater value to having an alien moral and political setup for it rather than &quot;sometimes you become an asshole&quot; which is really what the random swapping stuff ends up saying. It doesn't make the other side seem as important to the Dreaming its really just asshole Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, it's not random as presented in the Nunnehi writeup; it's not a thing they do &quot;just because&quot;. While some Nunnehi remain Winter long-term, the switch to Winter is more usually done in response to being recently angered or insulted. When a Nunnehi switches to Summer, they go through a purifying or cleansing ritual, signifying that they've let go of their darker side (or their trickster side) for the time being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:46:40-07:00","id":668241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=668087#post668087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read all of the Unseelie code very differently, I guess. It strikes me more as an individualistic, non-hierarchical code.<br /> <br /> 'Glamour is free' means, to me, that Glamour should belong to everyone. Glamour shouldn't be rationed and hoarded. It should be shared and spent and used. However, I agree that Ravaging needs to be less objectively evil in the setting. It should be possible to Ravage someone but for them to recover and dream again. I'd perhaps make it more like Changeling: The Lost, where you can inspire an emotion in someone and feed off that, as a baser form of Glamour reaping. It's how wraiths feed (sort of), so it wouldn't be completely out of place in the setting. The side-effects for the victim could range from temporary madness to inertia to a deep, nightmarish sleep, so that there were still consequences, but ones which don't kill the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I liked about LARP changeling was how they described ravaging thresholds. It was less about destroying someone's ability to dream and more about instilling in them more negative emotions, you break someone out of their comfortable life by filling them with rage, or fear or whatever. THis lets you have more traditionally heroic Unseelie playing Batman or being political activists<br /> <br /> I would also change the focus abit from Glamour is free to Glamour is meant to be Free. Then play up the value of spreading it around like an investment or planting seeds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 'Honour is a lie' - well, it's kind of true, isn't it? Yes, oaths have an objective existence as magical ties to the Dreaming, but they're also a kind of voluntary servitude or even enslavement. Following an oath becomes less about honour, for me, and more about lack of freedom. You're coerced into following oaths, because there are serious metaphysical penalties for not doing so. True honour would be following a vow to someone or following a cause without supernatural forces pushing you to do so. I'd propose, instead, a system of vows to mirror the system of oaths. These would be agreements freely entered into, but which have no mechanical or metaphysical component. They're things the Unseelie want to do, rather than things they have to do. I'd have them be roleplaying concepts only (like Nature and Demeanour), but you could always allow them to provide social bonuses - especially if you port in the Social Combat rules from Dead Man's Party. </div> </div> </div>Tell a Troll Honor is a Lie, but ignoring the oaths thing this tenent is abit annoying because its not really a drive to be weird alien morality but rather &quot;be a cynical jerk&quot;. The Seelie comments on honor aren't just &quot;play chivaliric knight' but also between death before dishonor and never forget a debt plays the fairy stories where they do crazy alien things to Assuage their perception of honor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 'Passion before duty' is also a pretty Romantic, anti-authoritarian and highly individualistic concept. It reminds me of Crowley's tenet 'Do as thou wilt shall be the whole of the law'. In other words, do a thing because you feel passionately about it, and because you want to do it, not because of guilt, shame or moral obligation. That might seem selfish, and it probably is by most counts, but it's also being truer to yourself. There's a different kind of honour, subjectively, in being true to yourself and your own ideals, rather than to the status quo. For that reason, I'd recommend that Unseelie characters note down passions that they have. When following these passions, I'd give them the opportunity to regain Glamour or Willpower (to balance it out, I'd also reward the following of oaths with the same for Seelie characters). You could port in the Passions system from Wraith if you really wanted to get crunchy, otherwise you can just list three core passions and issue Glamour or Willpower as feels appropriate. (Another option might instead be to allow a reroll on any action that directly feeds or follows a passion.) </div> </div> </div>I might go so far as to give out Kith based passions, the HUNGER of a Redcap, the Tricksyness of a Pooka.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll say in general the problem with the Unseelie is they are.. well banal in litteral sense of the word, these are not statements of grand nightmares with alien thoughts and desires but rather simply understandable cynical acts. the Unseelie should be inspiring and beautiful in a horrific fashion not a cynical commentary and that's really all I get. Nothing alien nothing fae just sort of a vague parody of Republican politics...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T03:44:49-07:00","id":669444,"title":"","content":"I posted this to the wrong thread, so removed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Posted this to the wrong thread... 09-18-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T08:35:44-07:00","id":669730,"title":"","content":"So Lian what would your Unseelie Code be about? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T18:02:05-07:00","id":670350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=668236#post668236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, it's not random as presented in the Nunnehi writeup; it's not a thing they do &quot;just because&quot;. While some Nunnehi remain Winter long-term, the switch to Winter is more usually done in response to being recently angered or insulted. When a Nunnehi switches to Summer, they go through a purifying or cleansing ritual, signifying that they've let go of their darker side (or their trickster side) for the time being.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I mean by &quot;Asshole frenzy&quot; something that would cause a vampire or Werewolf to flip out and kill you makes you asshole until you go through a ritual to let it go. I'd much rather see less a &quot;this is natural&quot; because lets face it Ebola is natural, and more this is a valuable part of the Dreaming, show the dreams of WInter the importance of the Trickster not that &quot;people randomly flip to it so everyone has it&quot; because as I said every vampire frenzies too but most don't treat it as something awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=669730#post669730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Lian what would your Unseelie Code be about? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> -Change is Good-<br /> .<br /> -Banality must die-Glamour is good and all but banality is our enemy. Fight it. Kill it. Shatter people's perspectives.<br /> <br /> -Be True to your Dream-a Pooka tricks. a Red cap consumes. A Troll is Duty and a Sidhe dominates! You are carved from the Dream itself be what you should be!<br /> <br /> -There are dreams in the shadows too-Horror, pain, anger, sorrow are dreams or give birth to them as much as every act of beauty<br /> <br /> <br /> Not really solid on them but its my first draft.<br /> <br /> What i want to hit is Unseelie as Innovators, as driven by alien passions, as much more &quot;Out in the world&quot; vs the Seelie sitting off in their castles hidden the dream. There is a war to fight and the Dreaming is at stake. the Seelie in their stasis in their cowardice have betrayed the Dreaming, they have turned their back on the war to protect it to hide and play games. Fuck them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T00:03:43-07:00","id":670519,"title":"","content":"Which fits in with one of the Shadow Court themes about trying to build bridges with the prodigals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T14:55:59-07:00","id":671351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=670519#post670519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which fits in with one of the Shadow Court themes about trying to build bridges with the prodigals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> think of it like this. The Unseelie are the court of Autumn and Winter. They are the court of the Autumn World. They are in part about forcing the seeds of glamour on the autumn world and damn the consquences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T05:31:56-07:00","id":681952,"title":"","content":"Played an Ailil here, and perfectly comfortable with keeping the association of Unseelie and &quot;Evil&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T23:40:07-07:00","id":687972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=671351#post671351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> think of it like this. The Unseelie are the court of Autumn and Winter. They are the court of the Autumn World. They are in part about forcing the seeds of glamour on the autumn world and damn the consquences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like. It makes sense, and it gives them something to do besides twirl their mustaches, eat babies, and cackle at the thought of enslaving everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T22:15:34-07:00","id":690902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=667078#post667078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glamour is Free-Full stop this is bullshit. Its fundimentally runs up against the setting conceit of Glamour being rare and dying. This makes every Unseelie member at best wasteful in a dying world and this is before we point to Ravaging and Rapturing for litterally killing the Golden Goose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think this is profound. The Seelie believe that Glamour is rare and dying. The Unseelie don't. They believe it is everywhere because mortals will always find an outlet for their dreams and imagination. Yes, ravaging and rapturing is the dark side of this. But the positive side is a change in attitude - hope is alive, there is always a new child; there is always someone finding the artistic spirit in them; there is always that next sunrise tomorrow that is the most beautiful some mortal has ever seen. You just need to find it. Stop killing yourself with all this Seelie code crap.<br /> <br /> Have the Unseelie truly believe this, and not just as an excuse for ravaging. Instead, make them appear much more happier and hopeful than the Seelie. Unseelie are just the Yippies and tricksters of the Fae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=667078#post667078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Passion before duty-this one definately comes off as sinister but can be interpretted as benign, however much like Honor is a lie and Glamour is free it seems to fly in the face of setting rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>i actually think this is easy to get through. There are lots of duties people have that may not make sense. In the Iliad there is a scene where Hector tells his wife that he is going out to fight Achilles and will die, and that is OK even though it means his family will be abandoned and god knows what will happen to you. In WWII, there were a lot of German officer who wanted to kill Hitler but thought it would be wrong because they swore an oath of personal loyalty - just too bad about those millions of people being murdered and their country going to be destroyed. In real life, every day people put up with all sorts of ridiculous rules, duties, and obligations over those things they feel are more important, except they need to do it.<br /> <br /> It is very easy for the Unseelie to say, &quot;Hey, all that is bullshit. You are being used by others. Do what you know is right, do what you want to do.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T23:26:16-07:00","id":690925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=690902#post690902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually think this is profound. The Seelie believe that Glamour is rare and dying. The Unseelie don't. They believe it is everywhere because mortals will always find an outlet for their dreams and imagination. Yes, ravaging and rapturing is the dark side of this. But the positive side is a change in attitude - hope is alive, there is always a new child; there is always someone finding the artistic spirit in them; there is always that next sunrise tomorrow that is the most beautiful some mortal has ever seen. You just need to find it. Stop killing yourself with all this Seelie code crap.<br /> <br /> Have the Unseelie truly believe this, and not just as an excuse for ravaging. Instead, make them appear much more happier and hopeful than the Seelie. Unseelie are just the Yippies and tricksters of the Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the game didn't portray it as objectively wrong, it wouldn't be an issue. That's my problem with it. Not that they can't profoundly believe it but really the option given is &quot;hey here's a faction that's completely and utterly wrong and use it to justify being evil&quot;<br /> <br /> That was where I started at. Now they could rework the whole system and make ravaging not objectively destroying the Dreaming by each little bit.<br /> <br /> But I also think there should be a place for horror, madness, anger, grief things that are not beautiful but dreamed off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> i actually think this is easy to get through. There are lots of duties people have that may not make sense. In the Iliad there is a scene where Hector tells his wife that he is going out to fight Achilles and will die, and that is OK even though it means his family will be abandoned and god knows what will happen to you. In WWII, there were a lot of German officer who wanted to kill Hitler but thought it would be wrong because they swore an oath of personal loyalty - just too bad about those millions of people being murdered and their country going to be destroyed. In real life, every day people put up with all sorts of ridiculous rules, duties, and obligations over those things they feel are more important, except they need to do it.<br /> <br /> It is very easy for the Unseelie to say, &quot;Hey, all that is bullshit. You are being used by others. Do what you know is right, do what you want to do.&quot; </div> </div> </div>of course its easy. Its too damned easy. Its boringly easy banally easy. Its just a cynical counter reaction to the Seelie. That I think is my big problem with the Unseelie court Its not itsown thing. All its tenents are just cynical responses to the Seelie. I really feel it should grow in a different direction to offer variety. Really there doesn't need to be a court of cynicism because that's just banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T04:20:52-07:00","id":691025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=690925#post690925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the game didn't portray it as objectively wrong, it wouldn't be an issue. That's my problem with it. Not that they can't profoundly believe it but really the option given is &amp;quot;hey here's a faction that's completely and utterly wrong and use it to justify being evil&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> That was where I started at. Now they could rework the whole system and make ravaging not objectively destroying the Dreaming by each little bit.<br /> <br /> But I also think there should be a place for horror, madness, anger, grief things that are not beautiful but dreamed off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> of course its easy. Its too damned easy. Its boringly easy banally easy. Its just a cynical counter reaction to the Seelie. That I think is my big problem with the Unseelie court Its not itsown thing. All its tenents are just cynical responses to the Seelie. I really feel it should grow in a different direction to offer variety. Really there doesn't need to be a court of cynicism because that's just banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think those things are Banal at all. I agree Ravaging should be more like the MET system, so that it doesn't actually destroy the Dreaming but does have risks. But other than that, Passion Before Honour and Glamour is Free are perfectly good tenets to believe.<br /> <br /> There may not be much Glamour left in the world, but that doesn't mean you shouldn't take what's there or try to create more. Is Glamour dwindling because the Seelie accept that it is and should be rare? If more fae were Unseelie, perhaps we'd see it flow like a torrent.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Passion Before Honour isn't objectively wrong. Yes, the system rewards honour, but just because something is rewarded, doesn't make it right. Following your passions has its own different rewards. Arguably, binding yourself to another 'because rules' is rather static anyway, and feeds the status quo. Wouldn't it be ironic if the Dreaming, in supporting honour and oaths, is actually calcifying itself in this respect? Freedom has its own kind of dynamism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T15:54:48-07:00","id":691767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=691025#post691025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think those things are Banal at all. I agree Ravaging should be more like the MET system, so that it doesn't actually destroy the Dreaming but does have risks. But other than that, Passion Before Honour and Glamour is Free are perfectly good tenets to believe.<br /> <br /> There may not be much Glamour left in the world, but that doesn't mean you shouldn't take what's there or try to create more. Is Glamour dwindling because the Seelie accept that it is and should be rare? If more fae were Unseelie, perhaps we'd see it flow like a torrent.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Passion Before Honour isn't objectively wrong. Yes, the system rewards honour, but just because something is rewarded, doesn't make it right. Following your passions has its own different rewards. Arguably, binding yourself to another 'because rules' is rather static anyway, and feeds the status quo. Wouldn't it be ironic if the Dreaming, in supporting honour and oaths, is actually calcifying itself in this respect? Freedom has its own kind of dynamism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its not the Seelie who claim that Glamor is dwindling. Its an explicit part of the game. Its such a fundimental premise up there with &quot;you play fairies in the modern world'. Glamour is dwindling is why the characters are changelings and not true fae. Its why there was a Sundering and a Shattering. Its why the Sidhe abandoned the world for 600 years<br /> <br /> You are hitting my argument against &quot;Honor is a lie&quot; when talking about Passion before Duty. My problem with Passion before Duty is that its trite. &quot;Do whatever you want wahooo freedom!&quot; is well just trite advice and seems to merely be a reaction to the values of honor and duty placed on the Seelie. It comes off not as profound but as teenage cynicism. It doesn't come off to me as advice to be grand but rather small and petty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T08:04:57-07:00","id":692480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=691767#post691767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its not the Seelie who claim that Glamor is dwindling. Its an explicit part of the game. Its such a fundimental premise up there with &quot;you play fairies in the modern world'. Glamour is dwindling is why the characters are changelings and not true fae. Its why there was a Sundering and a Shattering. Its why the Sidhe abandoned the world for 600 years<br /> <br /> You are hitting my argument against &quot;Honor is a lie&quot; when talking about Passion before Duty. My problem with Passion before Duty is that its trite. &quot;Do whatever you want wahooo freedom!&quot; is well just trite advice and seems to merely be a reaction to the values of honor and duty placed on the Seelie. It comes off not as profound but as teenage cynicism. It doesn't come off to me as advice to be grand but rather small and petty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the fluff could be better (another instance of CTD not being clear about what kind of game it it), but, from the Unseelie perspective, if the fae accept that Glamour is scarce and that's the way it should be, that's admitting defeat. 'Glamour is Free' is more a statement of defiance, a reflection on ownership and the sharing of resources, and a rallying call than a statement of objective fact. Besides which, even if Glamour is scarce, it can still be free--it belongs to everyone, and to no one; it's for sharing and using, rather than hoarding. Yes, the setting makes that hard, but real-life rebellion is hard too.<br /> <br /> The mindframe behind the Unseelie is rather anarchist in many ways (and perhaps libertarian too, in the right light). For the Unseelie, accepting the status quo perpetuates the status quo. Refusing to accept it might lead to change.<br /> <br /> This may be idealistic or even naive, but that's what activists and campaigners and dreamers and poets do every day. That's a perfectly acceptable mindframe for a changeling. It doesn't matter if it's in the setting, OOC. IC, it's perfectly fine for changeling characters to treat Glamour as if it's something they can seed and share and spread if only they imagine they can. This is a game about imagining more and defying what's 'real' anyway. It makes sense that the Unseelie are wilfully denying the 'real' to create their own 'truth' (see: Mage, the Consensus, etc).<br /> <br /> Likewise with Passion Before Honour, I don't see it as immature (even though it would be considered such according to most contemporary Western perceptions). I mentioned Aleister Crowley earlier, because the root of his philosophy was: 'Do as thou wilt shall be the whole of the law.' A very similar tenet. You or I may not agree with that philosophy, but it's a detailed and nuanced one that underpins a lot of contemporary magickal theory. It makes sense for a game about faeries to draw upon ideologies like these, rather than trying to make them understandable by everyday human standards.<br /> <br /> Passion Before Honour isn't about being irresponsible, per se. It can be, yes, but it can also mean, 'Trust your own judgement to do what you feel is the right thing to do (even if &quot;right&quot; here means &quot;evil&quot;), rather than blindly following the rules because The Boss knows best.' I just think the setting needs to elucidate these things a bit better, rather than leaving us to debate them because they're not clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 10-07-2015, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:06:54-07:00","id":692537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=692480#post692480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that the fluff could be better (another instance of CTD not being clear about what kind of game it it), but, from the Unseelie perspective, if the fae accept that Glamour is scarce and that's the way it should be, that's admitting defeat. 'Glamour is Free' is more a statement of defiance, a reflection on ownership and the sharing of resources, and a rallying call than a statement of objective fact. Besides which, even if Glamour is scarce, it can still be free--it belongs to everyone, and to no one; it's for sharing and using, rather than hoarding. Yes, the setting makes that hard, but real-life rebellion is hard too.<br /> <br /> The mindframe behind the Unseelie is rather anarchist in many ways (and perhaps libertarian too, in the right light). For the Unseelie, accepting the status quo perpetuates the status quo. Refusing to accept it might lead to change.<br /> <br /> This may be idealistic or even naive, but that's what activists and campaigners and dreamers and poets do every day. That's a perfectly acceptable mindframe for a changeling. It doesn't matter if it's in the setting, OOC. IC, it's perfectly fine for changeling characters to treat Glamour as if it's something they can seed and share and spread if only they imagine they can. This is a game about imagining more and defying what's 'real' anyway. It makes sense that the Unseelie are wilfully denying the 'real' to create their own 'truth' (see: Mage, the Consensus, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I don't think &quot;Glamour is Free&quot; pushes this mindset vs &quot;RAVAGING IS KEWL CAUSE FUCK THA MAN!&quot;. I want Horror, I want Chaos. I want Unseelie to be about taking it to Banality rather than being about &quot;accepting&quot; it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise with Passion Before Honour, I don't see it as immature (even though it would be considered such according to most contemporary Western perceptions). I mentioned Aleister Crowley earlier, because the root of his philosophy was: 'Do as thou wilt shall be the whole of the law.' A very similar tenet. You or I may not agree with that philosophy, but it's a detailed and nuanced one that underpins a lot of contemporary magickal theory. It makes sense for a game about faeries to draw upon ideologies like these, rather than trying to make them understandable by everyday human standards.<br /> <br /> Passion Before Honour isn't about being irresponsible, per se. It can be, yes, but it can also mean, 'Trust your own judgement to do what you feel is the right thing to do (even if &quot;right&quot; here means &quot;evil&quot;), rather than blindly following the rules because The Boss knows best.' I just think the setting needs to elucidate these things a bit better, rather than leaving us to debate them because they're not clear. </div> </div> </div>You know its possible to Find Crowley, Rand, and Levey Trite right? Its not that I am unfamiliar with these concepts.These are not weird alien concepts, they are not mind blowing concepts that people in western culture have no idea about. I find &quot;Do as thou wilt&quot; &quot;Follow your dreams&quot; &quot;You're free&quot; useless statements these are the base action this is how people are without needing to be told anything, people will intrinsically want to do what they want. There's no psychological drive for duty, only perhaps fear so there's no real conflict in &quot;passion before duty&quot; and that's my problem with it.<br /> <br /> Its also really easy to come up with bizare bits of honor because we've had thousands of years of people doing that than alien passions, if there were more bits of alien passions I might see that but when the majority of fairy tale &quot;monsters&quot; require the Seelie code to make sense maybe the Unseelie code has kind of failed hard?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T10:06:44-07:00","id":692651,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I should be wading into this conversation, so I'll leave the rest of it alone. I do want to say something about one thing though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=692537#post692537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no psychological drive for duty</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans are incredibly social creatures. We are pretty much hardwired to form groups. Part of that is empathy and supporting people outside of the individual - the basis of duty.<br /> <br /> Glamour comes from the higher order human thoughts and emotions, both positive and negative. Honor, duty, and standing among one's peers is part of glamour, so is rebellion, shirking responsibility, and forging one's own path.<br /> <br /> The two courts embody the extremes of human psychology, so while death before dishonor and passion before duty are polar opposites and almost no individual will ever always embody one to the exclusion of the other, they are both valid psychologically and are equally glamorous.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T15:33:49-07:00","id":692999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=692651#post692651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I should be wading into this conversation, so I'll leave the rest of it alone. I do want to say something about one thing though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Humans are incredibly social creatures. We are pretty much hardwired to form groups. Part of that is empathy and supporting people outside of the individual - the basis of duty.<br /> <br /> Glamour comes from the higher order human thoughts and emotions, both positive and negative. Honor, duty, and standing among one's peers is part of glamour, so is rebellion, shirking responsibility, and forging one's own path.<br /> <br /> The two courts embody the extremes of human psychology, so while death before dishonor and passion before duty are polar opposites and almost no individual will ever always embody one to the exclusion of the other, they are both valid psychologically and are equally glamorous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Death before dishonor, is crazy.You'd never get that as advice from someone. You'd never get &quot;Never forget a debt' as advice. But &quot;Follow your heart&quot; that you'll get. And that's all Passion before Duty is but made &quot;Edgy&quot;. Fairies are creatures of cosmic madness, they are stories given form. Safe, reasonable, sane these are and should be the buzzwords the call of banality. So I think ultimately Passion before Duty needs to be ramped up, it needs to be something more something insane,<br /> <br /> :Let your Passions consume you.<br /> <br /> If Seelie are willing to die over honor, the Unseelie should be willing to die for their passions. When the Joker tries to make Batman break to the point he would let himself die just to &quot;win&quot; that's what should be here. When Malificent takes a slight social faux pas as an excuse to lay down a curse on an entire kingdom? Even to the point that it ultimately destroys her, even to the point that the sane thing would be to ignore it, that should be there.<br /> <br /> That's my vision of the Unseelie. Not as cynical counter point to the Seelie. Not as fifth column for banality or the Formorians but a grand and gloriously dark part of the Dream. Something necissary, something important and something that has been betrayed by the Seelie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T05:17:51-07:00","id":693772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=692999#post692999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death before dishonor, is crazy.You'd never get that as advice from someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seppuku is an actual thing that actually happened, as are kamikaze pilots and suicide bombers. It's not usually ritualized these days, but people will still commit suicide over perceived personal failures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=692999#post692999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd never get &quot;Never forget a debt' as advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must live in a very different world from you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T10:06:34-07:00","id":693987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=692999#post692999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Death before dishonor, is crazy.You'd never get that as advice from someone. You'd never get &quot;Never forget a debt' as advice. But &quot;Follow your heart&quot; that you'll get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Follow your heart? Solipsistic non-advice espoused by Disney characters devoid of real wisdom or insight. What has value, what can be depended upon? The shifting lusts and hungers of the self, or bonds of oath or clan? In many cultures a sense of duty is very compelling, as Pooka Knight mentioned. I could never see a shogun tell his samurai &quot;follow your heart.&quot; &quot;Death before dishonor&quot; is quite fitting and certainly has its place in various factions of the OWoD. In these societies, you would do far better to depend on the honor of your kin than on some misplaced personal desire.<br /> <br /> What you describe is almost the tenants that the Black Spiral Dancers ascribe to, now that I think about it. Unseelie seem to have more going on than unbridled passion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-08-2015, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T16:03:45-07:00","id":694265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=693772#post693772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seppuku is an actual thing that actually happened, as are kamikaze pilots and suicide bombers. It's not usually ritualized these days, but people will still commit suicide over perceived personal failures.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason why the 47 ronin is considered a truly spectacular thing, because most people WEREN'T making that push. Suicide was generally used as an honorable out vs execution. It wasn't &quot;Go on and live with dishonor or kill yourself&quot; it was &quot;Kill yourself and die with honor or be killed and don't&quot;. Kamakazes weren't the first, second or even third line plan. They were the last. They were the point of complete despiration when the Japanese were losing.<br /> <br /> But hey, people taking that to 11 is perfectly reasonable and common vs &quot;Follow your heart&quot; right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I must live in a very different world from you. </div> </div> </div>You've never been told to &quot;just let shit go&quot; that's what never forget a debt means, Every slight. Every rage you never. Ever let go. There is no Mercy. There is no Forgiveness there is only what they owe you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=693987#post693987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Follow your heart? Solipsistic non-advice espoused by Disney characters devoid of real wisdom or insight. What has value, what can be depended upon? The shifting lusts and hungers of the self, or bonds of oath or clan? In many cultures a sense of duty is very compelling, as Pooka Knight mentioned. I could never see a shogun tell his samurai &quot;follow your heart.&quot; &quot;Death before dishonor&quot; is quite fitting and certainly has its place in various factions of the OWoD. In these societies, you would do far better to depend on the honor of your kin than on some misplaced personal desire.<br /> <br /> What you describe is almost the tenants that the Black Spiral Dancers ascribe to, now that I think about it. Unseelie seem to have more going on than unbridled passion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I find &quot;passion before duty&quot; solipsistic non advice made &quot;edgy&quot; so it doesn't look like the clear disneyism it is. And there were a lot more Shoguns who told their samurai &quot;Death before dishonor&quot; who had them route than had them die for him, that should say something about how well it was recieved, but you know &quot;passion before duty&quot; right?(MY desire to live over my duty to my shogun!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T16:30:56-07:00","id":694312,"title":"","content":"Lian, are you speaking in character from the perspective of an unseelie?<br /> <br /> I'm not being snarky. I honestly can't tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T18:50:28-07:00","id":695579,"title":"","content":"oocly but I think it might be best to start from some basic premises.<br /> <br /> 1. Seelie and Unseelie should be valid ways to &quot;Good&quot; guys.<br /> <br /> I find this is undercut by setting points that treat them either as 5th column for banality(as they dwell in it more readily have no problem using iron etc) and for the Formorians(Thalain, House balor), I find this is undercut by the willingness to Ravage when the setting basically says &quot;Yep that kills the dreaming&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2. I feel that banality should have its lure for changelings. The Dreaming is about narrative logic and tropes it wants you to do elaborate death traps then walk away. Banality is about cutting through that and sometimes just wanting to machine gun a person down. The seductive quality of banality is its easy, its sane, its smart.<br /> <br /> 3. With number 2 as a premise I don't feel the Unseelie should be the fail state of the Seelie. Failing to live up to the Code shouldn't be a &quot;Fall&quot; to the Unseelie. Too much of the Unseelie code reads to me as a fail state for the Seelie. I think rather being a dishonorable person who shits on beauty and love should be a Seelie embracing banality rather than unseelie nature.<br /> <br /> 4. Currently there's no real lure for an Unseelie fae to &quot;fall&quot; to their seelie nature.<br /> <br /> This is why I don't feel the Unseelie Code works currently. It seems to be just completely at odds with basic premises of the setting. Both in its pro Ravaging stance, to in my mind being almost an active addherent to banality. I want something that pushes rather accepts whatever action may come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T18:49:28-07:00","id":696728,"title":"","content":"I have no problem with Unseelie largely being EVIL<br /> <br /> would prefer anything to create unseelie good guys be in a sidebar or optional rule<br /> <br /> I do feel however that Glamour is not good<br /> <br /> Banality is not evil.<br /> <br /> the Fae fight for glamour and against banality for their own survival<br /> <br /> A parent who is very strict and domineering might be high banality but be genuinely loving in their fashioin<br /> <br /> A deranged Serial killer might have LOW Banality but be EVIL","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T23:03:32-07:00","id":696789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=696728#post696728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no problem with Unseelie largely being EVIL<br /> <br /> would prefer anything to create unseelie good guys be in a sidebar or optional rule</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Unseelie=Evil&quot; just doesn't work.<br /> <br /> 1. Seelie get a full range of options. I mean Look at Doctor Doom he's pretty much the perfect example of Seelie villainry. Death Before Dishonor! Never Forget a Debt! Sure he doesn't play up everything but The code is something to aspire to not something everyone lives up to perfectly.<br /> <br /> 2. The Unseelie being evil validates their complete repression, no only on a political scale but makes someone giving into to their Unseelie nature being the equivalent of giving into your Shadow in Wraith. This is especially true when they are treated as a 5th column for Banality or the Formorians.<br /> <br /> 3. Having a mixed Motley/oath circle is rather expected having someone completely on a different page can be extremely problematic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do feel however that Glamour is not good<br /> <br /> Banality is not evil.<br /> <br /> the Fae fight for glamour and against banality for their own survival<br /> <br /> A parent who is very strict and domineering might be high banality but be genuinely loving in their fashioin<br /> <br /> A deranged Serial killer might have LOW Banality but be EVIL </div> </div> </div>You're missing out on Bedlam. Changelings who fall too much to the dreaming fall to madness. Those who push to far into banality become undone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T14:27:07-07:00","id":697917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=696789#post696789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Unseelie=Evil&amp;quot; just doesn't work.<br /> <br /> 1. Seelie get a full range of options. I mean Look at Doctor Doom he's pretty much the perfect example of Seelie villainry. Death Before Dishonor! Never Forget a Debt! Sure he doesn't play up everything but The code is something to aspire to not something everyone lives up to perfectly.<br /> <br /> 2. The Unseelie being evil validates their complete repression, no only on a political scale but makes someone giving into to their Unseelie nature being the equivalent of giving into your Shadow in Wraith. This is especially true when they are treated as a 5th column for Banality or the Formorians.<br /> <br /> 3. Having a mixed Motley/oath circle is rather expected having someone completely on a different page can be extremely problematic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're missing out on Bedlam. Changelings who fall too much to the dreaming fall to madness. Those who push to far into banality become undone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being good or evil doesn't have the same importance in fae circles. Being fae-like, however that manifests, is more important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T18:27:59-07:00","id":698263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/666436-just-one-changeling-wish-fix-the-unseelie-image?p=697917#post697917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being good or evil doesn't have the same importance in fae circles. Being fae-like, however that manifests, is more important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings are as much fae as humans, pushing too far towards your fae end drives you crazy. So they will have human biases, but purely from a fae perspective lets look over why &quot;EVIL&quot; is a shitty role.<br /> <br /> 1. If seelie can do anything what's the point of the Unseelie? This is a metagame perspective what is the point of having Unseelie for if everything is covered by various degrees of interpretation of the seelie code and banality and glamour? They are treated as equal and valid points, they should be given equal and valid development options.<br /> <br /> 2. Being the tool of banality means its perfectly right to wipe them out. It undercuts a major point of repression in setting. It also makes them litterally enemies of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> 3. Being the Tools of the Formorians makes them litterally betrayers of all things Fae. So once again its completely justifiable to wipe them out.<br /> <br /> 4. Lets move to just simple logic here. the Unseelie provide no benefit. They are dishonorable. They are cowardly. They are bullies. They are litteral parasites on the Dreaming murdering it. Why should they be given quarter? Why should they be accepted? Why shouldn't they be fought until their very end? Why shouldn't &quot;Falling to the Unseelie&quot; be treated like a Shadow in Wraith something that is the natural flaw in the soul that needs to be fought at every breath?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So tell me why should they exist either from a Game role perspective or an In universe explanation? Why isn't it right and just to mind rape every Unseelie with Sovereign clockwork orange style? Because that's what pointlessly evil gets you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T13:47:08-07:00","id":698935,"title":"","content":"I agree with the Unseelie should be stop to being inherently evil from the game's perspective. I always thinked about them as simply a different facet of ideas and stories and kinda like their code. It's passionate, individual, freedom-centric. In my eyes this is as much legit as chivalry, ruling and debts. I would like if in the new edition, both will be treated as equals, showing the good and bad possible outcomes of both codes. <br /> <br /> After all, If the technocracy, sabbat, or possibly the most close to them, the anarchs have good sides and very bad sides, why the courts shouldna't have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}